#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Founderizer hub.

One small file: tasks, questions, decisions, timers, a board and a practice
site. Python standard library only. A throwaway test kit, not the product.

Run it on the always-on machine:

    python3 hub.py

It listens on the hub machine's address from team.json ("addresses"). A name is
accepted only from that agent's own machine, and a name whose machine has no
address is refused wherever team.json pins any agent's machine to one. An agent with a
key (owner API 1.12) also sends that key on its helper routes, and its sessions
send their own session credential on their MCP routes; on a machine with several
agents the address alone names nobody. An agent without a key, alone on its address, keeps
the address rule, and owner routes use only the owner's address. Keys and
credentials do not separate processes of one OS user, so keep the hub on a
private (Tailscale) network.
"""
